      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im looking into opening a small coffee shop in a rural area where rent and living costs are pretty low. i'm seeing news about these new minimum wage hikes being proposed. how do these kinds of laws usually play out for small businesses in places like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "New minimum wage laws often pose a significant financial challenge for rural small businesses with already thin profit margins and low operational costs. While these rules promote fairness by raising the standard of living, they can force many small coffee shops to reduce staff hours, implement part-time-only roles, or increase the price of their coffee just to cover the increased labor expenses. Ultimately, the long-term impact depends on how quickly a local economy can absorb these higher wage expectations without driving one of the most valuable jobs in the area to the ground.",
